/// * The candidate's bytes in `ws` must hold an odd number of exactly `bits` bits, big-endian.
/// * `rand` must contain independent uniform random octets for the probabilistic interpretation. They are not secret under this contract.
/// * The size's scratch ranges of `ws` are unspecified on return.
/// * `ws` and `used` must not overlap each other or `rand` (distinct Rust objects never do).
/// * None of `ws`, `rand` and `used` may overlap the return address on the stack or the 184 bytes of stack below it, or wrap around the end of the address space (no Rust object does).
